{"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/Secuura/Distributed_Secuura/pulls/1427", "id": 4783019143, "node_id": "PR_kwDORcHGMc8AAAABHRcUhw", "html_url": "https://github.com/Secuura/Distributed_Secuura/pull/1427", "diff_url": "https://github.com/Secuura/Distributed_Secuura/pull/1427.diff", "patch_url": "https://github.com/Secuura/Distributed_Secuura/pull/1427.patch", "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/Secuura/Distributed_Secuura/issues/1427", "number": 1427, "state": "open", "locked": false, "title": "KS 1274: job 04 fails a scan when trivy reports neither Results nor ArtifactName", "user": {"login": "kksecura", "id": 258699643, "node_id": "U_kgDOD2txew", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/258699643?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/kksecura", "html_url": "https://github.com/kksecura", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/kksecura/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/kksecura/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/kksecura/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/kksecura/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/kksecura/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/kksecura/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/kksecura/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/kksecura/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/kksecura/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "body": "Refs KS-1274 \u2014 https://linear.app/secuura/issue/KS-1274/job-04-a-trivy-that-exits-0-with-a-bare-still-reads-as-a-clean-image\n\nRaised from a Wednesday-held Spark pass, re-proved by Seat R 18th on develop `0a6177ea5482`.\n\n## What this changes\n\nA trivy that exits **0** and prints a bare `{}` was recorded as a **clean image**. KS 1136 already\ncovered a non-zero exit and output `jq` could not read; it did not cover a well-formed *empty*\nobject \u2014 the one shape where \"no vulnerabilities\" and \"no scan happened\" are indistinguishable from\nthe artefact.\n\n`Blockchain/Testing/jobs/04-container-trivy.sh:115-120` now records `scan-failed` when trivy's\nstdout carries **neither** `Results` **nor** `ArtifactName`.\n\n**Both keys must be absent, and that is deliberate.** The ticket's own suggested fix \u2014 fail on a\nmissing `Results` \u2014 over-fires: a genuinely clean image can report `ArtifactName` with no `Results`\narray, and failing it would turn every clean scan into an error. So the ticket's suggestion is *not*\nwhat landed. The suite pins the distinction with a control cell that is green in the patched state\nand in the reverted state alike.\n\nThe three trivy suites stubbed a clean image as `{}`, which under the new guard is precisely the\nfailure case. The stub moves to `{\"Results\":[]}` **in this same commit**, and `fail.txt` gains the\n`bare` and `nores` vocabulary so each shape can be produced deliberately.\n\nBoth platform-k HTML docs are updated in this same commit per SKILL \u00a74: flow block `35.`, cheat\nsection keyed to this ticket.\n\n## Test Evidence\n\n**Touched**\n- `Blockchain/Testing/jobs/04-container-trivy.sh` (product; mode `100755` preserved \u2014 verified by\n  `ls-tree` on the commit, and `diff --raw` base\u2192head reads `:100755 100755`)\n- `Blockchain/Dev/scripts/__tests__/container_trivy_failed_scan_is_loud.test.sh`\n- `Blockchain/Dev/scripts/__tests__/container_trivy_exit_code_env_keeps_findings.test.sh`\n- `Blockchain/Dev/scripts/__tests__/container_trivy_image_filter.test.sh`\n- `Projects Documents/API_Security_Functional_Testing_Architecture_Flow_Diagrams.html`\n- `Projects Documents/QA_Tool_Cheat_Sheet_Secuura_API_Testing.html`\n\n**Ran** (host: macOS arm64, node v24.7.0, npm 11.5.1, bash **3.2.57**, typescript 5.9.3)\n- `container_trivy_failed_scan_is_loud.test.sh` \u2192 **5 passed, 0 failed**\n- `container_trivy_exit_code_env_keeps_findings.test.sh` \u2192 **6 passed, 0 failed**\n- `container_trivy_image_filter.test.sh` \u2192 **5 passed, 0 failed**\n- **RED proof** \u2014 product reverted to the base blob with the suites kept patched:\n  **4 passed, 1 failed, rc 1**. The single failure is the new cell\n  `\ud83d\udd34 KS-1274 a trivy that exits 0 with a bare {} is recorded as scan-failed and the job exits 1`.\n  The `ArtifactName and no Results stays clean` control passed in **both** states, so the tamper is\n  specific rather than a blanket break. Product restored byte-identical\n  (sha256/16 `b0a19e77c940633c`).\n- S-1 installs: `npm ci --ignore-scripts` in `Blockchain/Dev` (1937 packages, rc 0);\n  `npm run build --workspace=packages/shared` rc 0 with `dist/index.js` asserted present\n  (17,746 B); `npm ci` in all four `systemTest/*` (akto 255, api-explorer 219, performance 145,\n  playwright 124 packages). **0 tracked files modified after S-1.**\n\n**NOT run**\n- **A live scan. This is the material gap.** This host has no docker daemon and no trivy binary, so\n  every cell runs against stubs on a private `PATH`. The real scanner's bare-`{}` behaviour is\n  **UNMEASURED here** \u2014 the guard is proved against the stub's reproduction of it, not against\n  trivy itself. **A live run is owed and this ticket does not move to Done.**\n- The four platform suites (Schemathesis, Akto, Playwright, Performance/k6) \u2014 no local stack, so\n  they were not run and no result is claimed for them.\n- `bash >= 4.1` behaviour: this host is **3.2.57**, so nothing here exercises a 4.x/5.x errexit path.\n- Runner versions read from `node_modules`: vitest 5.0.3 (akto, api-explorer, performance),\n  @playwright/test 1.63.0. **Engines gap, wider than previously recorded:** `akto`,\n  `performance` **and** `playwright` each declare `engines.node >= 24.11.0` while this host runs\n  **v24.7.0**, so all three installed below their declared floor and emitted `EBADENGINE`.\n  `api-explorer` declares no engines. Nothing in this PR depends on those four packages.\n\n**Migrations + config**\n- **None.** No migration, no dependency, lockfile, manifest, baseline or spec-version edit. No\n  `.env` touched. No per-slot literal introduced.\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n", "created_at": "2026-10-08T06:52:01Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-08T06:52:06Z", "closed_at": null, "merged_at": null, "merge_commit_sha": "03fa19fbfab2c9d4413c661fa85af22ca33910fb", "assignees": [], "requested_reviewers": [], "requested_teams": [], "labels": [], "milestone": null, "draft": false, "commits_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/Secuura/Distributed_Secuura/pulls/1427/commits", "review_comments_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/Secuura/Distributed_Secuura/pulls/1427/comments", "review_comment_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/Secuura/Distributed_Secuura/pulls/comments{/number}", "comments_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/Secuura/Distributed_Secuura/issues/1427/comments", "statuses_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/Secuura/Distributed_Secuura/statuses/2b6da5f561b05a820bbe1ab5e891bff9f4f531c8", "head": {"label": "Secuura:feature/ks-1274-trivy-bare-object-guard-ra18-1", "ref": "feature/ks-1274-trivy-bare-object-guard-ra18-1", "sha": "2b6da5f561b05a820bbe1ab5e891bff9f4f531c8", "user": {"login": "Secuura", "id": 257240886, "node_id": "O_kgDOD1UvNg", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/257240886?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/Secuura", "html_url": "https://github.com/Secuura", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Secuura/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Secuura/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Secuura/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Secuura/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Secuura/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Secuura/orgs"